      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The community sits beside Arkabutla Lake, a 20,000‑acre reservoir on the Coldwater River built by the U.S. Army Corps of Engineers in 1943.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/Arkabutla,_Mississippi",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Anglers flock to Arkabutla Lake for its renowned crappie and catfish, though low water levels since 2023 have temporarily limited fishing access.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/Arkabutla,_Mississippi",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Arkabutla lies in Mississippi’s Lower Alluvial Valley, where gentle 0‑2% slopes and silty alluvium create expansive bottomland floodplains.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13,
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/Arkabutla,_Mississippi",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The area enjoys a humid climate, with January lows around 31°F, July highs near 92°F, and about 56 inches of rain each year.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19,
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/Arkabutla,_Mississippi",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "vague"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Ecologically, Arkabutla Lake supports diverse habitats—from bottomland hardwoods to open wetlands—providing hunting for waterfowl and hosting a wildlife rehabilitation center.",
